Scan, then hand the findings to a coding agent as one fix prompt

Usage: android-doctor fix [OPTIONS] <INPUT>

Arguments:
  <INPUT>  Directory to scan (same input as `doctor scan`)

Options:
      --agent <AGENT>  Agent to launch if its binary is on PATH [default: claude] [possible values: claude, codex, cursor]
      --no-color       Never emit colour, even on a terminal (also honours the NO_COLOR environment variable)
      --print          Only print the prompt; launch nothing
      --safe           Keep the agent's approval prompts (already the default)
      --yolo           Launch the agent with its approval prompts skipped (unsafe: the firmware is untrusted)
  -h, --help           Print help
